{"id":"FIG-01f45dfa34841411","src":"figure","doc":"AUTOSAR_SWS_OS","page":95,"text":"","caption":"Figure 9.3: Protection Hook sequence chart The sequence shows the flow of control if a protection error occurs. Depending on the return values of the ProtectionHook, either the faulty Task/OsIsr is forcibly terminated or the OS-Application is forcibly terminated or the system is shut down. If the action is to terminate the faulty OS-Application an option is to start afterwards the restart task, which can do a cleanup, etc.","sha":"01f45dfa348414113a3b0cfc528e946b2a5c874d4d50740923c2e2b8d753a121","series":[{"id":"FIG-01f45dfa34841411","releases":["R3.0.7","R3.1.5","R3.2.3"],"sha":"01f45dfa348414113a3b0cfc528e946b2a5c874d4d50740923c2e2b8d753a121"}],"releases":["R3.0.7","R3.1.5","R3.2.3"],"occurrences":[{"release":"R3.0.7","doc":"AUTOSAR_SWS_OS","page":95,"pdf":"R3.0.7/AUTOSAR/CLASSIC/AUTOSAR_SWS_OS.pdf"},{"release":"R3.1.5","doc":"AUTOSAR_SWS_OS","page":95,"pdf":"R3.1.5/AUTOSAR/CLASSIC/AUTOSAR_SWS_OS.pdf"}],"kind":"figure","platform":"classic","targets":[{"role":"constitutive","conf":0.95,"rt":"","m":"gemini-3.8-flash","why":"ProtectionHook interface definition","rel":[],"id":"SWS_Os_00538"},{"role":"heuristic","conf":0.9,"rt":"","m":"gemini-3.8-flash","why":"ProtectionHook returns PRO_TERMINATETASKISR","rel":[],"id":"SWS_Os_00553"},{"role":"heuristic","conf":0.9,"rt":"","m":"gemini-3.8-flash","why":"ProtectionHook returns PRO_TERMINATEAPPL","rel":[],"id":"SWS_Os_00554"},{"role":"heuristic","conf":0.9,"rt":"","m":"gemini-3.8-flash","why":"ProtectionHook returns PRO_TERMINATEAPPL_RESTART","rel":[],"id":"SWS_Os_00555"},{"role":"heuristic","conf":0.8,"rt":"","m":"gemini-3.8-flash","why":"ProtectionHook action and termination","rel":[],"id":"SWS_Os_00243"}],"ok":true,"schema":"versions-explorer@1"}